          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order confirmed; event-level conclusion blocked\n\nThe relevant manufacturing order is **MO-25-09-1070**, corresponding to **WO-2025-09-004** for the **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine DeKoven operation.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Work order | **WO-2025-09-004 / MO-25-09-1070** |\n| September cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Not available |\n| Event amount | Not available |\n| Exact event-created time | Not available |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not available |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event record |\n\nThe accessible Task records contain work-order and cost-period rows, but **no cost-event rows**. Supporting records returned **“not staged,”** and access to the supporting package was denied. Consequently, I cannot establish whether a late event occurred. **This is not a finding that no late event occurred.** The Pending Close timestamp above is reproduced exactly; the source supplies no time-zone offset.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nThe supplied Oracle 26B documentation states that newly created transactions falling in the Pending Close period or an earlier period **are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting** and are processed after the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, even if in error. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions that continue processing.**\n\nThus, evaluating the recorded status requires the event’s type, creation timestamp, and accounting status—not merely the work order’s creation or completion date.\n\n**Sources:** Task records, `work_orders` and `cost_periods`; *Oracle Supply Chain Cost Management 26B*, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225.\n\nNo database records were changed. The incomplete report was submitted with state **`needs_evidence`**, and the audit result and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_7db8dc5c7410/audit-report.json`.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
